Object.assign(window.__CMPDATA__=window.__CMPDATA__||{},{"mysql__14": "<div class=\"lang-block lang-zh\"><div class=\"cell-main\"><span class=\"verdict v-partial\">部分支持</span><p class=\"snippet\">社区版/企业版（Oracle）：无公开的国测/信创认证信息；等保合规由部署方测评 待验证。 各云厂商的托管 MySQL（RDS 等）继承云厂商的等保三级/可信云资质 厂商口径。 国际：Oracle 云体系的 SOC2/ISO 等适用于 Oracle 运营的 MySQL HeatWave 云服务 厂商口径。</p><div class=\"full\" hidden><span class=\"verdict v-partial\">部分支持</span><ul>\n<li>社区版/企业版（Oracle）：无公开的国测/信创认证信息；等保合规由部署方测评 <span class=\"ev ev-tbd\" data-zh=\"待验证\" data-en=\"to-be-verified\">待验证</span>。</li>\n<li>各云厂商的托管 MySQL（RDS 等）继承云厂商的等保三级/可信云资质 <span class=\"ev ev-vendor\" data-zh=\"厂商口径\" data-en=\"vendor claim\">厂商口径</span>。</li>\n<li>国际：Oracle 云体系的 SOC2/ISO 等适用于 Oracle 运营的 MySQL HeatWave 云服务 <span class=\"ev ev-vendor\" data-zh=\"厂商口径\" data-en=\"vendor claim\">厂商口径</span>。</li>\n</ul></div></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"cell-toggle\" data-zh=\"展开\" data-en=\"Expand\">展开</button></div><div class=\"lang-block lang-en\" hidden><div class=\"cell-main\"><span class=\"verdict v-neutral\">full section</span><p class=\"snippet\">Non-standard dimension format in this profile; expand to see the full section.</p><div class=\"full\" hidden><h3>1. Data-at-rest encryption (TDE) — Partially supported</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Supported: InnoDB tablespace data-at-rest encryption with a two-level key hierarchy (tablespace key stored in the tablespace header, encrypted by the master key; master key rotation supported) <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>. Coverage: tablespaces, doublewrite, system tablespace, redo, undo; binlog/relay log and audit log encryption each require separate configuration <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>All editions (including Community) ship a local file-based keyring (<code>component_keyring_file</code> / <code>keyring_file</code>); Enterprise additionally provides encrypted password-protected key files, KMIP, Oracle Key Vault, AWS KMS and other keyring backends <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Community Edition has tablespace encryption, but <strong>a local file keyring is not a compliance-grade external KMS/HSM</strong>; losing the key means the data is unrecoverable <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>TDE does not protect in-memory data, authorized SQL users, or data in transit <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Cloud hosting caveat: RDS/Aurora MySQL do not support MySQL&#x27;s native keyring/TDE and instead use cloud-disk KMS encryption — this is a cloud-offering difference, not a MySQL kernel deficiency <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>2. Transport encryption (TLS) — Supported</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>TLS connections supported, with certificate and cipher configuration; MySQL 8.4 removed TLS 1.0/1.1 <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>The full <code>caching_sha2_password</code> authentication flow requires a secure connection (TLS) or RSA key exchange; otherwise older clients may fail to connect — one of the most common causes of connection breakage when upgrading from 8.0 to 8.4 <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>3. Auditing — Partially supported (Enterprise dividing line)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The Enterprise Audit plugin (<code>audit_log</code>) is commercial-only</strong>; Community Edition has no official audit plugin <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Community alternatives: the general log (heavy performance overhead, unsuitable to leave on in production), binlog (records writes only, not reads), Percona Server&#x27;s free built-in Audit Log Plugin (configuration keys differ from the official one) <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Conclusion: for compliance auditing, Community Edition is &quot;workable but undignified&quot;; only Enterprise has a first-class solution.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>4. Authentication &amp; authorization — Supported (some Enterprise-only features)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Supported: <code>caching_sha2_password</code> (default since 8.0), roles, dynamic privileges (SUPER split into fine-grained privileges such as <code>SYSTEM_VARIABLES_ADMIN</code>) <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Since 8.4, <code>mysql_native_password</code> is disabled by default (separate dynamic plugin, requires explicit <code>--mysql-native-password=ON</code> to enable); old clients failing to connect after upgrade is the #1 pitfall <span class=\"ev ev-tested\" data-zh=\"社区实测\" data-en=\"community-tested\">社区实测</span> <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Enterprise-only: PAM, LDAP, Kerberos authentication; FIDO authentication was removed in 8.4 <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li><strong>Missing: row-level security (RLS)</strong>. MySQL has no PG-style RLS; multi-tenant isolation can only be implemented via views or the application layer <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>5. Backup &amp; recovery — Supported (complete but tiered tooling)</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Type</th><th>Suitable for</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><code>mysqldump</code></td><td>Logical</td><td>&lt;10GB, small DBs, cross-version migration</td><td>Single-threaded; slow backup, even slower restore for large DBs <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span></td></tr>\n<tr><td>MySQL Shell dump/load</td><td>Parallel logical</td><td>10GB+</td><td><code>mysqlpump</code> was removed in 8.4; this is the officially recommended replacement <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Percona XtraBackup</td><td>Physical hot backup</td><td>Large production DBs</td><td>Free, open source, incremental, fast restore; the de facto standard for Community Edition <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span></td></tr>\n<tr><td>MySQL Enterprise Backup</td><td>Physical hot backup</td><td>Large production DBs</td><td>Commercial-only <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Clone plugin</td><td>Physical clone</td><td>Fast replica provisioning / test environments</td><td>Built in, supports local and remote cloning <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span></td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>PITR: full backup + binlog replay; requires <code>log_bin</code> enabled and binlogs retained (expiration controlled by <code>binlog_expire_logs_seconds</code> in 8.4) <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Deep-water point: <strong>backup ≠ recovery capability</strong>. Logical backup restore is single-threaded SQL replay; for large DBs, RTO is measured in hours; physical backups require <code>--prepare</code>; a backup that has never been through a restore drill is just a wish <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>6. Observability — Supported (strong built-ins, but with an &quot;observability tax&quot;)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Available: <code>performance_schema</code> + <code>sys</code> schema (SQL digest, wait events, locks, IO, threads), slow query log, <code>SHOW ENGINE INNODB STATUS</code>, <code>data_locks</code> / <code>data_lock_waits</code>, <code>EXPLAIN ANALYZE</code> <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>The tax: the default instrument set is generally production-safe; <strong>enabling all instruments/consumers produces measurable overhead</strong>. LINE&#x27;s old benchmark saw roughly a 15% TPS drop with everything enabled in a specific sysbench scenario — this is a <strong>community-tested result on an old version under a specific workload and must not be generalized into a fixed number</strong> <span class=\"ev ev-tested\" data-zh=\"社区实测\" data-en=\"community-tested\">社区实测</span>.</li>\n<li>Setting the slow-log threshold too low produces significant IO overhead; <code>EXPLAIN ANALYZE</code> <strong>actually executes</strong> the statement — it cannot be used as a side-effect-free diagnostic for writes <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Correct posture: selective enablement normally, temporarily widened collection during incidents.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>7. Connection model — Supported (thread-per-connection; thread pool is Enterprise-only)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Default <strong>thread-per-connection</strong>: one OS thread per connection; <code>max_connections</code> defaults to 151 <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>The <strong>Thread Pool plugin is Enterprise-only</strong>; Percona Server provides a free <code>thread_pool</code> plugin as an alternative <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Deep-water point: per-connection memory cost is real (<code>sort_buffer_size</code>, <code>join_buffer_size</code>, etc. are allocated per connection); the community&#x27;s classic formula is &quot;1000 connections × 256MB sort buffer = 256GB upper bound&quot; <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>. Under connection storms, thread context switching drags the instance down; the production standard is a connection pooler in front (ProxySQL / MySQL Router / bounded application-side pools), with pool size typically set to <code>max_connections - 10</code> (reserving 10 for management and replication) <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>8. Transactions &amp; isolation levels — Supported (default RR + gap locks is a double-edged sword)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Default <code>REPEATABLE READ</code>; InnoDB uses record locks + gap locks + next-key locks to prevent phantom reads <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li><strong>INSERTs on different keys can also deadlock</strong> (insert intention checks the gap for locks, uniqueness checks take record locks, and reversed lock acquisition order forms a cycle); UPDATE/DELETE without an index locks row by row during the scan (not &quot;lock escalation&quot;, but a large number of row locks) <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Deadlock auto-detection rolls back one victim (error 1213); applications must catch it and <strong>retry the entire transaction</strong>; 1205 is lock wait timeout, different from deadlock <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Dropping to READ COMMITTED eliminates most gap locks, but cannot eliminate deadlocks caused by lock ordering, unique keys, or foreign keys <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Long/large transactions: see Deep Dives.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>9. Replication &amp; consistency — Supported (async default; HA has a gradient)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Default <strong>asynchronous replication</strong>: the primary commits without waiting for replicas; failover can lose unapplied transactions, RPO &gt; 0 <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>GTID + <code>SOURCE_AUTO_POSITION=1</code> simplifies replica re-pointing, but <strong>GTID is not a zero-loss guarantee</strong>; compare <code>Executed_Gtid_Set</code> before promoting a replica <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Semi-sync <code>AFTER_SYNC</code>: trades roughly one network RTT for a stronger durability guarantee of acknowledged commits; <code>AFTER_COMMIT</code> is not equivalent to zero loss <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Group Replication: built-in replication group / failover; but the certification process <strong>does not see gap locks</strong> (multi-primary mode officially recommends READ COMMITTED), has transaction size limits, requires tables to have primary keys (tables without PKs are not writable inside a group), InnoDB Cluster is officially <strong>LAN-only</strong> (cross-WAN writes suffer noticeably), and multi-datacenter deployments should use InnoDB ClusterSet (async links) <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Read scale-out: replicas scale reads only, not writes; <code>Seconds_Behind_Source</code> has blind spots such as idle resets, and the community recommends cross-checking with heartbeat/GTID monitoring <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>10. Scaling — Partially supported (no native auto-sharding)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Vertical: single-node scale-up (big memory, big NVMe is MySQL&#x27;s comfort zone).</li>\n<li>Horizontal read: async replicas, Group Replication, InnoDB Cluster.</li>\n<li>Horizontal write: <strong>no native auto-sharding</strong>. Rely on middleware such as Vitess / ShardingSphere / ProxySQL, or application-level sharding <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>NDB Cluster (MySQL Cluster) is a separate product — memory-centric, niche to operate — excluded from conventional evaluation <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>11. Compatibility — Supported (the protocol is the de facto standard, but the family has diverged)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>The MySQL protocol + SQL dialect is the ecosystem de facto standard: drivers, ORMs, toolchains are the most complete <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Divergence reality: MariaDB has drifted far (GTID, system tables, optimizer behavior all incompatible in places); Aurora MySQL is wire-compatible but has a completely different storage engine (failure behavior and performance characteristics cannot be assumed transferable); Percona Server tracks upstream closely and is basically &quot;MySQL + patches&quot; <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>12. License &amp; business model — Supported (clear dual track)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Community: GPLv2, feature-complete but without official audit / thread pool / enterprise-grade keyring backends / PAM-LDAP / commercial backup tools <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Enterprise Edition: commercial subscription, includes the above enterprise plugins + MySQL Enterprise Monitor + official support (LTS: Premier 5 years + Extended 3 years) <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Cloud: MySQL HeatWave (managed MySQL on OCI/AWS + in-memory acceleration/Lakehouse), Oracle&#x27;s flagship cloud narrative <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>13. Chinese-language materials — Partially supported</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>No Chinese version of the official documentation <span class=\"ev ev-tbd\" data-zh=\"待验证\" data-en=\"to-be-verified\">待验证</span> (no evidence of official Chinese docs found; whether to mark this &quot;verified absent&quot; vs &quot;not found&quot; needs reconfirmation — temporarily marked to-be-verified).</li>\n<li>Chinese community materials are abundant (blogs, columns, translations), but lagging behind 8.4/9.x new features is the norm <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr/>\n<h3>14. Performance &amp; latency — Supported (single-node OLTP benchmark; write scaling via sharding)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Point lookups/short transactions: tens of thousands of QPS per node in sysbench point-select, P99 in milliseconds (hardware/tuning dependent) <span class=\"ev ev-tested\" data-zh=\"社区实测\" data-en=\"community-tested\">社区实测</span>.</li>\n<li>Read scaling via async replicas; single-node write ceiling — scale writes with sharding middleware (ShardingSphere/DBLE) or application sharding <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Bottlenecks: large transactions, long DDL (8.0 Instant DDL helps some cases), oversized single tables <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>15. Compliance &amp; certifications — Partially supported (no official certs for open source; compliance via deployer or cloud)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Community/Enterprise editions (Oracle): no public information on Chinese national testing/trusted-innovation certification; MLPS (等保) compliance is the deployer&#x27;s responsibility <span class=\"ev ev-tbd\" data-zh=\"待验证\" data-en=\"to-be-verified\">待验证</span>.</li>\n<li>Managed MySQL offerings inherit their cloud provider&#x27;s MLPS Level 3 / Trusted Cloud qualifications <span class=\"ev ev-vendor\" data-zh=\"厂商口径\" data-en=\"vendor claim\">厂商口径</span>.</li>\n<li>International: Oracle Cloud&#x27;s SOC2/ISO family covers Oracle-operated MySQL HeatWave cloud service <span class=\"ev ev-vendor\" data-zh=\"厂商口径\" data-en=\"vendor claim\">厂商口径</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>16. Maturity &amp; community — Supported (released 1995; among the most mature open-source RDBMS)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Released 1995; joined Oracle via Sun in 2010; 8.0/8.4 LTS plus 9.x innovation releases <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Tens of thousands of GitHub stars; the thickest ecosystem (drivers, tools, tutorials) <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Risk: Oracle&#x27;s stewardship periodically sparks community-vs-enterprise feature-split controversies <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>17. Notable adopters — Supported (the bedrock of big internet companies)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Public heavy users include Meta (Facebook) and Wikipedia <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Once powered early YouTube/Twitter/Uber architectures; some later migrated <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>China: in-house MySQL forks at major internet companies (Alibaba/Tencent) are the de-facto standard <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>18. Ecosystem tooling — Supported (most complete: backup/migration/CDC/monitoring)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Backup: mysqldump, MySQL Shell, XtraBackup, Clone plugin <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Online DDL/migration: gh-ost, pt-online-schema-change <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>CDC: Debezium, Canal; monitoring: PMM, mysqld_exporter + Prometheus <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>19. Managed &amp; serverless — Supported (RDS on every cloud; PlanetScale does serverless)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>RDS on every cloud vendor (Alibaba/Tencent/AWS/Huawei) <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Oracle MySQL HeatWave (cloud-native + analytics acceleration) <span class=\"ev ev-vendor\" data-zh=\"厂商口径\" data-en=\"vendor claim\">厂商口径</span>.</li>\n<li>Serverless: PlanetScale (serverless MySQL on Vitess) <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>20. Data ingestion — Supported (LOAD DATA/mysqlimport; mydumper; mysqlsh)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>LOAD DATA INFILE and mysqlimport are the fastest single-node load paths <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>mydumper/myloader for parallel logical import/export, community mainstream <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>mysqlsh util.loadDump parallel-loads MySQL Shell dumps <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>21. External data access — Partially supported (FEDERATED engine is weak; no modern external tables)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>The FEDERATED engine maps remote MySQL tables but is weak in features/performance, rarely used in prod <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>No direct S3/object-storage or lakehouse-format querying <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>MySQL HeatWave offers object-storage queries as a commercial capability <span class=\"ev ev-vendor\" data-zh=\"厂商口径\" data-en=\"vendor claim\">厂商口径</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>22. CDC &amp; downstream — Supported (Row binlog has the most mature ecosystem: Debezium/Canal/Maxwell)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Row-format binlog is the de-facto CDC source <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Debezium, Canal, Maxwell and Flink CDC are all mature <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>GTID + semisync make position management easy; huge transactions bloat binlog <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>23. TTL &amp; data lifecycle — Partial (Partition exchange + events; no native row-level TTL)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Partitioned tables + scheduled events dropping partitions is the production standard <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>No native row-level TTL; big-table DELETEs are slow and generate heavy undo/redo <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>24. Online DDL &amp; schema evolution — Partial (Limited InnoDB online DDL; gh-ost/pt-osc ecosystem)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>InnoDB online DDL: many add-column cases are online, but type/PK/charset changes still rebuild and lock <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Production standard for huge tables is gh-ost/pt-online-schema-change — watch replica lag and trigger risks <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>8.0 instant add column only covers trailing columns; limited scope <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>25. Multi-tenancy &amp; resource isolation — Partial (Limited resource groups; CPU affinity only)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>8.0 resource groups do thread CPU affinity/priority; no memory/IO throttling <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Production multi-tenancy means multiple instances; noisy neighbors are common on shared ones <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>26. Cross-region active-active — Partial (Cross-region replicas configurable; dual-write conflicts unsolved)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Primary-replica / Group Replication can span regions; latency follows the network <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>No native conflict resolution for dual-write active-active; off-limits in production <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Group Replication is latency-sensitive across regions <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>27. HA &amp; RTO/RPO — Partial (MHA / MGR / InnoDB Cluster; many but fragmented options)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>MHA manual/semi-auto cutover: minutes of RTO with split-brain risk <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>MGR/InnoDB Cluster fail over natively in seconds-to-minutes but are complex to run <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Semi-sync keeps RPO≈0; async can lose data <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>28. Row-level security &amp; masking — Partial (No native RLS; Enterprise has masking)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Community Edition has no native row-level security; row isolation relies on views, stored procedures, or app-layer WHERE filters, which are easy to bypass <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span></li>\n<li>MySQL Enterprise Edition ships a Data Masking and De-Identification component that masks fields at SELECT time (e.g. mask_pan) <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span></li>\n<li>Column-level GRANT SELECT(col) exists, but there is no dynamic masking policy engine <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span></li>\n<li>Main cost risk: full masking capability is tied to the commercial edition <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>29. JSON &amp; semi-structured — Supported (Native JSON + virtual-column indexes)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Native binary JSON, -&gt;&gt;/JSON_TABLE, indexes via virtual generated columns <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>No direct JSON indexes (need virtual columns); big JSON updates rewrite whole column <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>30. Full-text search — Supported (FULLTEXT + ngram CJK)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>FULLTEXT with ngram parser for Chinese <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Simple relevance; weaker than ES at scale <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>31. Storage efficiency &amp; compression — Supported (InnoDB page + transparent compression, full feature set)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>InnoDB supports page compression (KEY_BLOCK_SIZE 1/2/4/8K) and transparent page compression (punch hole), reducing disk footprint at row level. <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span></li>\n<li>Barracuda file format with DYNAMIC/COMPRESSED row formats improves storage density for large objects. <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span></li>\n<li>Compression adds CPU overhead; the ratio-vs-performance tradeoff on write-heavy workloads should be measured in practice. <code>(community tested)</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>32. OSS license &amp; lock-in risk — Not supported (GPL open source; mature MariaDB/Percona forks)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>MySQL Community Edition is open source under GPLv2; source is freely available for self-hosting. <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span></li>\n<li>Oracle holds the MySQL trademark and copyright, but long-lived forks (MariaDB, Percona Server) provide mature drop-in alternatives, keeping migration cost low. <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span></li>\n<li>Oracle enterprise plugins and MySQL HeatWave cloud services carry commercial licensing and cloud-binding constraints; moving back to self-hosting removes them. <span class=\"ev ev-vendor\" data-zh=\"厂商口径\" data-en=\"vendor claim\">厂商口径</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>33. Optimizer &amp; plan stability — Supported (CBO + rich hints; no plan freeze, flips common)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>CBO + EXPLAIN with rich hints (STRAIGHT_JOIN, FORCE INDEX, SET_VAR, QB_NAME) <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Weak histogram statistics; no Oracle-style plan baseline freeze <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Stale statistics/parameter changes causing plan flips are a common production issue <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>34. Tuning &amp; autonomy — Partial (Hundreds of params; strong performance_schema)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Hundreds of tunable parameters; tuning complexity is DBA consensus <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>performance_schema + sys schema give a complete diagnostic stack <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>No auto-indexing/rewrites; weak autonomy <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>35. Silent corruption protection — Supported (InnoDB checksums plus doublewrite)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>InnoDB pages carry checksums verified on read; corrupt pages are rejected outright. <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span></li>\n<li>The doublewrite buffer guards against torn pages after a crash, a key link in silent-corruption defense. <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span></li>\n<li>Replication copies pages verbatim, so corruption can spread silently without external checksum tools. <code>(community tested)</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>36. Stored procedures &amp; triggers — Supported (SPs/triggers; weak language)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Full procedures, triggers, event scheduler <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>No packages, weak debugging; Oracle PL/SQL rewrites costly <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>37. Constraints &amp; integrity — Supported (Full InnoDB FK/CHECK)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>InnoDB FKs, enforced CHECK (8.0.16+), unique constraints <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>FKs add locks and cascade write amplification; use carefully at scale <code>(community tested)</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>38. Analytical SQL — Supported (8.0 windows/CTEs; not analytic)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>8.0 window functions, CTEs (incl. recursive) <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Optimizer weak on complex analytics; big joins/sorts slow <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>39. Right to erasure — Partial (Manual DELETE; no erasure attestation)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>DELETE is a row-level hard delete (InnoDB reclaims space; in-page residue can be overwritten), but there is no right-to-erasure workflow or attestation <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span></li>\n<li>Binlog, redo log, and backups retain historical copies of deleted rows; physical erasure requires log rotation and fresh backups with no automation <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span></li>\n<li>GDPR practice is usually logical delete plus periodic physical cleanup, or DROP TABLE on partitions for bulk erasure <code>(community tested)</code></li>\n<li>Replication widens the residue surface: replicas and delayed standbys stay readable inside the delete-lag window <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>40. Data lineage &amp; catalog — Not supported (Verified: no native lineage)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>No native data lineage/catalog <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Third parties like Atlas/DataHub harvest binlog/metadata <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>41. Storage-compute architecture — Supported (Coupled: local-disk InnoDB)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Classic coupled design: InnoDB data on local disks <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>HeatWave&#x27;s disaggregation is Oracle-cloud-only, not in the OSS edition <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>42. Multi-model — Partial (JSON + full-text; no vector/graph)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>JSON type with multi-valued indexes/generated columns; full-text indexes available <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>No native vector or graph <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>43. FinOps &amp; cost observability — N/A (No metering; hardware plus labor)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>MySQL has no built-in metering; costs are servers, storage, and operations labor. <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span></li>\n<li>Managed cloud editions (RDS, Aurora, etc.) expose cost attribution through cloud billing tags and budget alerts. <span class=\"ev ev-vendor\" data-zh=\"厂商口径\" data-en=\"vendor claim\">厂商口径</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>44. Drivers &amp; clients — Supported (Widest driver ecosystem: full Connector family)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Official Connector/J, Connector/NET, Connector/Python, mysqlclient <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Broadest ORM/tool support in the industry <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>45. Materialized views — Not supported (Verified absent; summary tables)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>No materialized views (verified absent) <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Summary tables + triggers/jobs; consistency on you <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>46. Multi-cloud support — Supported (Open source on any cloud; no binding)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Open source deploys on any cloud/self-hosted; no vendor binding <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Cloud RDS offerings are similar; moving clouds is mostly logical migration <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul></div></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"cell-toggle\" data-zh=\"展开\" data-en=\"Expand\">Expand</button></div>", "mysql__15": "<div class=\"lang-block lang-zh\"><div class=\"cell-main\"><span class=\"verdict v-yes\">有</span><p class=\"snippet\">1995 年发布，2010 年随 Sun 并入 Oracle；8.0/8.4 LTS、9.x 创新版并行 社区共识。 GitHub stars 万级，生态（驱动/工具/教程）最厚 社区共识。 风险点：Oracle 主导下社区版与企业版功能分界时有争议 社区共识。</p><div class=\"full\" hidden><span class=\"verdict v-yes\">有</span><ul>\n<li>1995 年发布，2010 年随 Sun 并入 Oracle；8.0/8.4 LTS、9.x 创新版并行 <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>。</li>\n<li>GitHub stars 万级，生态（驱动/工具/教程）最厚 <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>。</li>\n<li>风险点：Oracle 主导下社区版与企业版功能分界时有争议 <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>。</li>\n</ul></div></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"cell-toggle\" data-zh=\"展开\" data-en=\"Expand\">展开</button></div><div class=\"lang-block lang-en\" hidden><div class=\"cell-main\"><span class=\"verdict v-neutral\">full section</span><p class=\"snippet\">Non-standard dimension format in this profile; expand to see the full section.</p><div class=\"full\" hidden><h3>1. Data-at-rest encryption (TDE) — Partially supported</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Supported: InnoDB tablespace data-at-rest encryption with a two-level key hierarchy (tablespace key stored in the tablespace header, encrypted by the master key; master key rotation supported) <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>. Coverage: tablespaces, doublewrite, system tablespace, redo, undo; binlog/relay log and audit log encryption each require separate configuration <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>All editions (including Community) ship a local file-based keyring (<code>component_keyring_file</code> / <code>keyring_file</code>); Enterprise additionally provides encrypted password-protected key files, KMIP, Oracle Key Vault, AWS KMS and other keyring backends <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Community Edition has tablespace encryption, but <strong>a local file keyring is not a compliance-grade external KMS/HSM</strong>; losing the key means the data is unrecoverable <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>TDE does not protect in-memory data, authorized SQL users, or data in transit <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Cloud hosting caveat: RDS/Aurora MySQL do not support MySQL&#x27;s native keyring/TDE and instead use cloud-disk KMS encryption — this is a cloud-offering difference, not a MySQL kernel deficiency <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>2. Transport encryption (TLS) — Supported</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>TLS connections supported, with certificate and cipher configuration; MySQL 8.4 removed TLS 1.0/1.1 <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>The full <code>caching_sha2_password</code> authentication flow requires a secure connection (TLS) or RSA key exchange; otherwise older clients may fail to connect — one of the most common causes of connection breakage when upgrading from 8.0 to 8.4 <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>3. Auditing — Partially supported (Enterprise dividing line)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The Enterprise Audit plugin (<code>audit_log</code>) is commercial-only</strong>; Community Edition has no official audit plugin <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Community alternatives: the general log (heavy performance overhead, unsuitable to leave on in production), binlog (records writes only, not reads), Percona Server&#x27;s free built-in Audit Log Plugin (configuration keys differ from the official one) <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Conclusion: for compliance auditing, Community Edition is &quot;workable but undignified&quot;; only Enterprise has a first-class solution.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>4. Authentication &amp; authorization — Supported (some Enterprise-only features)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Supported: <code>caching_sha2_password</code> (default since 8.0), roles, dynamic privileges (SUPER split into fine-grained privileges such as <code>SYSTEM_VARIABLES_ADMIN</code>) <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Since 8.4, <code>mysql_native_password</code> is disabled by default (separate dynamic plugin, requires explicit <code>--mysql-native-password=ON</code> to enable); old clients failing to connect after upgrade is the #1 pitfall <span class=\"ev ev-tested\" data-zh=\"社区实测\" data-en=\"community-tested\">社区实测</span> <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Enterprise-only: PAM, LDAP, Kerberos authentication; FIDO authentication was removed in 8.4 <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li><strong>Missing: row-level security (RLS)</strong>. MySQL has no PG-style RLS; multi-tenant isolation can only be implemented via views or the application layer <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>5. Backup &amp; recovery — Supported (complete but tiered tooling)</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Type</th><th>Suitable for</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><code>mysqldump</code></td><td>Logical</td><td>&lt;10GB, small DBs, cross-version migration</td><td>Single-threaded; slow backup, even slower restore for large DBs <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span></td></tr>\n<tr><td>MySQL Shell dump/load</td><td>Parallel logical</td><td>10GB+</td><td><code>mysqlpump</code> was removed in 8.4; this is the officially recommended replacement <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Percona XtraBackup</td><td>Physical hot backup</td><td>Large production DBs</td><td>Free, open source, incremental, fast restore; the de facto standard for Community Edition <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span></td></tr>\n<tr><td>MySQL Enterprise Backup</td><td>Physical hot backup</td><td>Large production DBs</td><td>Commercial-only <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Clone plugin</td><td>Physical clone</td><td>Fast replica provisioning / test environments</td><td>Built in, supports local and remote cloning <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span></td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>PITR: full backup + binlog replay; requires <code>log_bin</code> enabled and binlogs retained (expiration controlled by <code>binlog_expire_logs_seconds</code> in 8.4) <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Deep-water point: <strong>backup ≠ recovery capability</strong>. Logical backup restore is single-threaded SQL replay; for large DBs, RTO is measured in hours; physical backups require <code>--prepare</code>; a backup that has never been through a restore drill is just a wish <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>6. Observability — Supported (strong built-ins, but with an &quot;observability tax&quot;)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Available: <code>performance_schema</code> + <code>sys</code> schema (SQL digest, wait events, locks, IO, threads), slow query log, <code>SHOW ENGINE INNODB STATUS</code>, <code>data_locks</code> / <code>data_lock_waits</code>, <code>EXPLAIN ANALYZE</code> <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>The tax: the default instrument set is generally production-safe; <strong>enabling all instruments/consumers produces measurable overhead</strong>. LINE&#x27;s old benchmark saw roughly a 15% TPS drop with everything enabled in a specific sysbench scenario — this is a <strong>community-tested result on an old version under a specific workload and must not be generalized into a fixed number</strong> <span class=\"ev ev-tested\" data-zh=\"社区实测\" data-en=\"community-tested\">社区实测</span>.</li>\n<li>Setting the slow-log threshold too low produces significant IO overhead; <code>EXPLAIN ANALYZE</code> <strong>actually executes</strong> the statement — it cannot be used as a side-effect-free diagnostic for writes <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Correct posture: selective enablement normally, temporarily widened collection during incidents.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>7. Connection model — Supported (thread-per-connection; thread pool is Enterprise-only)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Default <strong>thread-per-connection</strong>: one OS thread per connection; <code>max_connections</code> defaults to 151 <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>The <strong>Thread Pool plugin is Enterprise-only</strong>; Percona Server provides a free <code>thread_pool</code> plugin as an alternative <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Deep-water point: per-connection memory cost is real (<code>sort_buffer_size</code>, <code>join_buffer_size</code>, etc. are allocated per connection); the community&#x27;s classic formula is &quot;1000 connections × 256MB sort buffer = 256GB upper bound&quot; <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>. Under connection storms, thread context switching drags the instance down; the production standard is a connection pooler in front (ProxySQL / MySQL Router / bounded application-side pools), with pool size typically set to <code>max_connections - 10</code> (reserving 10 for management and replication) <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>8. Transactions &amp; isolation levels — Supported (default RR + gap locks is a double-edged sword)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Default <code>REPEATABLE READ</code>; InnoDB uses record locks + gap locks + next-key locks to prevent phantom reads <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li><strong>INSERTs on different keys can also deadlock</strong> (insert intention checks the gap for locks, uniqueness checks take record locks, and reversed lock acquisition order forms a cycle); UPDATE/DELETE without an index locks row by row during the scan (not &quot;lock escalation&quot;, but a large number of row locks) <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Deadlock auto-detection rolls back one victim (error 1213); applications must catch it and <strong>retry the entire transaction</strong>; 1205 is lock wait timeout, different from deadlock <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Dropping to READ COMMITTED eliminates most gap locks, but cannot eliminate deadlocks caused by lock ordering, unique keys, or foreign keys <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Long/large transactions: see Deep Dives.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>9. Replication &amp; consistency — Supported (async default; HA has a gradient)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Default <strong>asynchronous replication</strong>: the primary commits without waiting for replicas; failover can lose unapplied transactions, RPO &gt; 0 <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>GTID + <code>SOURCE_AUTO_POSITION=1</code> simplifies replica re-pointing, but <strong>GTID is not a zero-loss guarantee</strong>; compare <code>Executed_Gtid_Set</code> before promoting a replica <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Semi-sync <code>AFTER_SYNC</code>: trades roughly one network RTT for a stronger durability guarantee of acknowledged commits; <code>AFTER_COMMIT</code> is not equivalent to zero loss <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Group Replication: built-in replication group / failover; but the certification process <strong>does not see gap locks</strong> (multi-primary mode officially recommends READ COMMITTED), has transaction size limits, requires tables to have primary keys (tables without PKs are not writable inside a group), InnoDB Cluster is officially <strong>LAN-only</strong> (cross-WAN writes suffer noticeably), and multi-datacenter deployments should use InnoDB ClusterSet (async links) <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Read scale-out: replicas scale reads only, not writes; <code>Seconds_Behind_Source</code> has blind spots such as idle resets, and the community recommends cross-checking with heartbeat/GTID monitoring <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>10. Scaling — Partially supported (no native auto-sharding)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Vertical: single-node scale-up (big memory, big NVMe is MySQL&#x27;s comfort zone).</li>\n<li>Horizontal read: async replicas, Group Replication, InnoDB Cluster.</li>\n<li>Horizontal write: <strong>no native auto-sharding</strong>. Rely on middleware such as Vitess / ShardingSphere / ProxySQL, or application-level sharding <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>NDB Cluster (MySQL Cluster) is a separate product — memory-centric, niche to operate — excluded from conventional evaluation <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>11. Compatibility — Supported (the protocol is the de facto standard, but the family has diverged)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>The MySQL protocol + SQL dialect is the ecosystem de facto standard: drivers, ORMs, toolchains are the most complete <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Divergence reality: MariaDB has drifted far (GTID, system tables, optimizer behavior all incompatible in places); Aurora MySQL is wire-compatible but has a completely different storage engine (failure behavior and performance characteristics cannot be assumed transferable); Percona Server tracks upstream closely and is basically &quot;MySQL + patches&quot; <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>12. License &amp; business model — Supported (clear dual track)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Community: GPLv2, feature-complete but without official audit / thread pool / enterprise-grade keyring backends / PAM-LDAP / commercial backup tools <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Enterprise Edition: commercial subscription, includes the above enterprise plugins + MySQL Enterprise Monitor + official support (LTS: Premier 5 years + Extended 3 years) <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Cloud: MySQL HeatWave (managed MySQL on OCI/AWS + in-memory acceleration/Lakehouse), Oracle&#x27;s flagship cloud narrative <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>13. Chinese-language materials — Partially supported</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>No Chinese version of the official documentation <span class=\"ev ev-tbd\" data-zh=\"待验证\" data-en=\"to-be-verified\">待验证</span> (no evidence of official Chinese docs found; whether to mark this &quot;verified absent&quot; vs &quot;not found&quot; needs reconfirmation — temporarily marked to-be-verified).</li>\n<li>Chinese community materials are abundant (blogs, columns, translations), but lagging behind 8.4/9.x new features is the norm <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr/>\n<h3>14. Performance &amp; latency — Supported (single-node OLTP benchmark; write scaling via sharding)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Point lookups/short transactions: tens of thousands of QPS per node in sysbench point-select, P99 in milliseconds (hardware/tuning dependent) <span class=\"ev ev-tested\" data-zh=\"社区实测\" data-en=\"community-tested\">社区实测</span>.</li>\n<li>Read scaling via async replicas; single-node write ceiling — scale writes with sharding middleware (ShardingSphere/DBLE) or application sharding <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Bottlenecks: large transactions, long DDL (8.0 Instant DDL helps some cases), oversized single tables <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>15. Compliance &amp; certifications — Partially supported (no official certs for open source; compliance via deployer or cloud)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Community/Enterprise editions (Oracle): no public information on Chinese national testing/trusted-innovation certification; MLPS (等保) compliance is the deployer&#x27;s responsibility <span class=\"ev ev-tbd\" data-zh=\"待验证\" data-en=\"to-be-verified\">待验证</span>.</li>\n<li>Managed MySQL offerings inherit their cloud provider&#x27;s MLPS Level 3 / Trusted Cloud qualifications <span class=\"ev ev-vendor\" data-zh=\"厂商口径\" data-en=\"vendor claim\">厂商口径</span>.</li>\n<li>International: Oracle Cloud&#x27;s SOC2/ISO family covers Oracle-operated MySQL HeatWave cloud service <span class=\"ev ev-vendor\" data-zh=\"厂商口径\" data-en=\"vendor claim\">厂商口径</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>16. Maturity &amp; community — Supported (released 1995; among the most mature open-source RDBMS)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Released 1995; joined Oracle via Sun in 2010; 8.0/8.4 LTS plus 9.x innovation releases <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Tens of thousands of GitHub stars; the thickest ecosystem (drivers, tools, tutorials) <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Risk: Oracle&#x27;s stewardship periodically sparks community-vs-enterprise feature-split controversies <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>17. Notable adopters — Supported (the bedrock of big internet companies)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Public heavy users include Meta (Facebook) and Wikipedia <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Once powered early YouTube/Twitter/Uber architectures; some later migrated <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>China: in-house MySQL forks at major internet companies (Alibaba/Tencent) are the de-facto standard <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>18. Ecosystem tooling — Supported (most complete: backup/migration/CDC/monitoring)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Backup: mysqldump, MySQL Shell, XtraBackup, Clone plugin <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Online DDL/migration: gh-ost, pt-online-schema-change <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>CDC: Debezium, Canal; monitoring: PMM, mysqld_exporter + Prometheus <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>19. Managed &amp; serverless — Supported (RDS on every cloud; PlanetScale does serverless)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>RDS on every cloud vendor (Alibaba/Tencent/AWS/Huawei) <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Oracle MySQL HeatWave (cloud-native + analytics acceleration) <span class=\"ev ev-vendor\" data-zh=\"厂商口径\" data-en=\"vendor claim\">厂商口径</span>.</li>\n<li>Serverless: PlanetScale (serverless MySQL on Vitess) <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>20. Data ingestion — Supported (LOAD DATA/mysqlimport; mydumper; mysqlsh)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>LOAD DATA INFILE and mysqlimport are the fastest single-node load paths <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>mydumper/myloader for parallel logical import/export, community mainstream <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>mysqlsh util.loadDump parallel-loads MySQL Shell dumps <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>21. External data access — Partially supported (FEDERATED engine is weak; no modern external tables)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>The FEDERATED engine maps remote MySQL tables but is weak in features/performance, rarely used in prod <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>No direct S3/object-storage or lakehouse-format querying <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>MySQL HeatWave offers object-storage queries as a commercial capability <span class=\"ev ev-vendor\" data-zh=\"厂商口径\" data-en=\"vendor claim\">厂商口径</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>22. CDC &amp; downstream — Supported (Row binlog has the most mature ecosystem: Debezium/Canal/Maxwell)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Row-format binlog is the de-facto CDC source <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Debezium, Canal, Maxwell and Flink CDC are all mature <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>GTID + semisync make position management easy; huge transactions bloat binlog <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>23. TTL &amp; data lifecycle — Partial (Partition exchange + events; no native row-level TTL)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Partitioned tables + scheduled events dropping partitions is the production standard <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>No native row-level TTL; big-table DELETEs are slow and generate heavy undo/redo <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>24. Online DDL &amp; schema evolution — Partial (Limited InnoDB online DDL; gh-ost/pt-osc ecosystem)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>InnoDB online DDL: many add-column cases are online, but type/PK/charset changes still rebuild and lock <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Production standard for huge tables is gh-ost/pt-online-schema-change — watch replica lag and trigger risks <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>8.0 instant add column only covers trailing columns; limited scope <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>25. Multi-tenancy &amp; resource isolation — Partial (Limited resource groups; CPU affinity only)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>8.0 resource groups do thread CPU affinity/priority; no memory/IO throttling <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Production multi-tenancy means multiple instances; noisy neighbors are common on shared ones <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>26. Cross-region active-active — Partial (Cross-region replicas configurable; dual-write conflicts unsolved)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Primary-replica / Group Replication can span regions; latency follows the network <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>No native conflict resolution for dual-write active-active; off-limits in production <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>Group Replication is latency-sensitive across regions <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>27. HA &amp; RTO/RPO — Partial (MHA / MGR / InnoDB Cluster; many but fragmented options)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>MHA manual/semi-auto cutover: minutes of RTO with split-brain risk <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>MGR/InnoDB Cluster fail over natively in seconds-to-minutes but are complex to run <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Semi-sync keeps RPO≈0; async can lose data <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>28. Row-level security &amp; masking — Partial (No native RLS; Enterprise has masking)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Community Edition has no native row-level security; row isolation relies on views, stored procedures, or app-layer WHERE filters, which are easy to bypass <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span></li>\n<li>MySQL Enterprise Edition ships a Data Masking and De-Identification component that masks fields at SELECT time (e.g. mask_pan) <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span></li>\n<li>Column-level GRANT SELECT(col) exists, but there is no dynamic masking policy engine <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span></li>\n<li>Main cost risk: full masking capability is tied to the commercial edition <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>29. JSON &amp; semi-structured — Supported (Native JSON + virtual-column indexes)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Native binary JSON, -&gt;&gt;/JSON_TABLE, indexes via virtual generated columns <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>No direct JSON indexes (need virtual columns); big JSON updates rewrite whole column <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>30. Full-text search — Supported (FULLTEXT + ngram CJK)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>FULLTEXT with ngram parser for Chinese <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Simple relevance; weaker than ES at scale <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>31. Storage efficiency &amp; compression — Supported (InnoDB page + transparent compression, full feature set)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>InnoDB supports page compression (KEY_BLOCK_SIZE 1/2/4/8K) and transparent page compression (punch hole), reducing disk footprint at row level. <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span></li>\n<li>Barracuda file format with DYNAMIC/COMPRESSED row formats improves storage density for large objects. <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span></li>\n<li>Compression adds CPU overhead; the ratio-vs-performance tradeoff on write-heavy workloads should be measured in practice. <code>(community tested)</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>32. OSS license &amp; lock-in risk — Not supported (GPL open source; mature MariaDB/Percona forks)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>MySQL Community Edition is open source under GPLv2; source is freely available for self-hosting. <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span></li>\n<li>Oracle holds the MySQL trademark and copyright, but long-lived forks (MariaDB, Percona Server) provide mature drop-in alternatives, keeping migration cost low. <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span></li>\n<li>Oracle enterprise plugins and MySQL HeatWave cloud services carry commercial licensing and cloud-binding constraints; moving back to self-hosting removes them. <span class=\"ev ev-vendor\" data-zh=\"厂商口径\" data-en=\"vendor claim\">厂商口径</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>33. Optimizer &amp; plan stability — Supported (CBO + rich hints; no plan freeze, flips common)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>CBO + EXPLAIN with rich hints (STRAIGHT_JOIN, FORCE INDEX, SET_VAR, QB_NAME) <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Weak histogram statistics; no Oracle-style plan baseline freeze <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Stale statistics/parameter changes causing plan flips are a common production issue <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>34. Tuning &amp; autonomy — Partial (Hundreds of params; strong performance_schema)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Hundreds of tunable parameters; tuning complexity is DBA consensus <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n<li>performance_schema + sys schema give a complete diagnostic stack <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>No auto-indexing/rewrites; weak autonomy <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>35. Silent corruption protection — Supported (InnoDB checksums plus doublewrite)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>InnoDB pages carry checksums verified on read; corrupt pages are rejected outright. <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span></li>\n<li>The doublewrite buffer guards against torn pages after a crash, a key link in silent-corruption defense. <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span></li>\n<li>Replication copies pages verbatim, so corruption can spread silently without external checksum tools. <code>(community tested)</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>36. Stored procedures &amp; triggers — Supported (SPs/triggers; weak language)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Full procedures, triggers, event scheduler <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>No packages, weak debugging; Oracle PL/SQL rewrites costly <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>37. Constraints &amp; integrity — Supported (Full InnoDB FK/CHECK)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>InnoDB FKs, enforced CHECK (8.0.16+), unique constraints <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>FKs add locks and cascade write amplification; use carefully at scale <code>(community tested)</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>38. Analytical SQL — Supported (8.0 windows/CTEs; not analytic)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>8.0 window functions, CTEs (incl. recursive) <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Optimizer weak on complex analytics; big joins/sorts slow <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>39. Right to erasure — Partial (Manual DELETE; no erasure attestation)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>DELETE is a row-level hard delete (InnoDB reclaims space; in-page residue can be overwritten), but there is no right-to-erasure workflow or attestation <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span></li>\n<li>Binlog, redo log, and backups retain historical copies of deleted rows; physical erasure requires log rotation and fresh backups with no automation <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span></li>\n<li>GDPR practice is usually logical delete plus periodic physical cleanup, or DROP TABLE on partitions for bulk erasure <code>(community tested)</code></li>\n<li>Replication widens the residue surface: replicas and delayed standbys stay readable inside the delete-lag window <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>40. Data lineage &amp; catalog — Not supported (Verified: no native lineage)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>No native data lineage/catalog <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Third parties like Atlas/DataHub harvest binlog/metadata <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>41. Storage-compute architecture — Supported (Coupled: local-disk InnoDB)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Classic coupled design: InnoDB data on local disks <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>HeatWave&#x27;s disaggregation is Oracle-cloud-only, not in the OSS edition <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>42. Multi-model — Partial (JSON + full-text; no vector/graph)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>JSON type with multi-valued indexes/generated columns; full-text indexes available <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>No native vector or graph <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>43. FinOps &amp; cost observability — N/A (No metering; hardware plus labor)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>MySQL has no built-in metering; costs are servers, storage, and operations labor. <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span></li>\n<li>Managed cloud editions (RDS, Aurora, etc.) expose cost attribution through cloud billing tags and budget alerts. <span class=\"ev ev-vendor\" data-zh=\"厂商口径\" data-en=\"vendor claim\">厂商口径</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>44. Drivers &amp; clients — Supported (Widest driver ecosystem: full Connector family)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Official Connector/J, Connector/NET, Connector/Python, mysqlclient <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Broadest ORM/tool support in the industry <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>45. Materialized views — Not supported (Verified absent; summary tables)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>No materialized views (verified absent) <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Summary tables + triggers/jobs; consistency on you <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>46. Multi-cloud support — Supported (Open source on any cloud; no binding)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Open source deploys on any cloud/self-hosted; no vendor binding <span class=\"ev ev-official\" data-zh=\"官方文档\" data-en=\"official docs\">官方文档</span>.</li>\n<li>Cloud RDS offerings are similar; moving clouds is mostly logical migration <span class=\"ev ev-consensus\" data-zh=\"社区共识\" data-en=\"community consensus\">社区共识</span>.</li>\n</ul></div></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"cell-toggle\" data-zh=\"展开\" data-en=\"Expand\">Expand</button></div>"});